post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'

libfprint-goodix53x5 notice
===========================

This update changes the image preprocessing used to produce enrolled prints.
Fingerprints enrolled with an earlier build are NOT compatible with the new
matcher path and may stop verifying. You must delete and re-enroll:

  fprintd-delete "$USER"
  fprintd-enroll          # or use your desktop's fingerprint settings

This re-enrollment is a one-time requirement for this update; routine future
updates will not need it unless the preprocessing changes again.

The driver now detaches the cdc_acm kernel driver itself, so the old
/etc/udev/rules.d/91-goodix-fingerprint.rules unbind rule is obsolete. If you
added it manually, you can remove it.
EOF
}
